    "note": "HPE's own row, not the model name. The 1950 QuickSpecs (v10, 2018) JG963A Technical Specifications table prints \"PoE power 370 W PoE+\", maximum power rating 470 W, and \"When supplemented with the use of an HPE RPS1600 Redundant Power System, up to 800W of PoE+ can be supplied\" - the 800 W needs the separately sold JG136A RPS. I/O row: \"48 RJ-45 auto-negotiating 10/100/1000 PoE+ ports\", \"2 SFP+ fixed 1000/10000 SFP+ ports\", \"2 RJ-45 1/10GBASE-T ports\", plus \"Additional ports and slots: 1 RJ-45 console port to access limited CLI port\", which was missing from the model. The 48-port carries the same 370 W as the 24-port JG962A: doubling the port count did not double the power."
  },
